## Conventions

### Code Style

- TypeScript strict mode (`strict: true` in tsconfig.json)
- Named exports only (no default exports)
- Functional components with hooks
- Error boundaries around route segments

### Naming

- Files: kebab-case (`user-profile.tsx`)
- Components: PascalCase (`UserProfile`)
- Functions/variables: camelCase (`getUserProfile`)
- Constants: SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE (`MAX_RETRY_COUNT`)
- CSS custom properties: kebab-case (`--color-primary`)

### Git

- Conventional commits: `type(scope): description`
- Feature branches: `feat/{feature-name}`
- Co-authored: `Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>`

### Testing

- Vitest for unit and integration tests
- Playwright for E2E tests
- axe-core for accessibility validation
- Test files: `src/**/__tests__/*.test.ts` or `src/**/*.test.ts`
- Minimum 80% statement coverage, 70% branch coverage

## Architecture Rules

- Always use CSS custom properties from `design-system.css`. Never hardcode colors, spacing, or typography.
- Always use Context7 MCP for API documentation lookups. Never paste documentation into the conversation.
- Always read existing code before modifying. Understand the pattern before changing it.
- Reference files instead of inlining content. "Read design-system.css" not paste it.

## MCP Server Rules

- **Playwright MCP** is for interactive E2E debugging and visual verification. Use `npx playwright test` for running full test suites.
- **Supabase MCP** must NEVER be used against production data. Only use with development or staging project URLs.
- **Stripe MCP** must ALWAYS use test mode keys (`sk_test_*`). Never use live keys.
- **Graceful degradation**: If any MCP tool is unavailable, continue with standard approaches (Bash, grep, WebSearch, Context7). Never hard-fail on MCP unavailability.

